<h1>Packaging Conveyor Systems</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">A packaging conveyor system connects every machine on a packaging line, from fillers and sealers through case packers and palletizers to stretch wrappers and shipping docks. It moves product between machines, buffers product when one machine stops, changes lanes for multipacks, and handles elevation changes between floor and mezzanine equipment.</p>
<p>The system's job is to keep a single machine stoppage from shutting down the whole line. The table below shows which conveyor types do that work at each stage.</p>
<h2 id="types-heading">Conveyor Types in a Packaging Line</h2>
<p>Most packaging lines combine five or more conveyor types. The right type depends on product shape, weight, speed, and handling needs at each point in the line.</p>
